              {
                "uuid": "c3f63ab1-59d6-409a-8729-a0f1d2d1d143",
                "control-id": "SP_800_171_03.13.11",
                "description": "Data submitted to the Patient Intake API is encrypted under a customer-managed AWS KMS key (aws_kms_key.phi, automatic annual rotation enabled, 7-day deletion window). The starter's uploads bucket is moved from AWS-managed SSE-S3 to SSE-KMS with that CMK and S3 Bucket Keys (GAP-01). The DynamoDB submissions table is moved from the AWS-owned key to the same CMK via its server_side_encryption block (GAP-02). The evidence vault, CloudTrail bucket and the CloudTrail trail itself are encrypted with the same CMK. The Lambda role may use the key only through S3 and DynamoDB (kms:ViaService condition). The Rego policy sc_3_13_11_encryption fails the plan when any aws_s3_bucket has no aws_s3_bucket_server_side_encryption_configuration referencing it.",
                "props": [
