                "remarks": "Known limitations: (1) the policy checks that an SSE configuration exists, not that sse_algorithm is aws:kms with a CMK, so a plan reverting GAP-01 to AES256 (SSE-S3) would pass the gate; (2) no policy covers the DynamoDB table, so GAP-02 is closed in Terraform only; (3) the AWS provider does not set use_fips_endpoint, so API calls use the standard (non-FIPS) service endpoints; (4) one CMK serves workload data, audit logs and evidence. Separate keys per data class are planned (see WRITEUP.md)."
              },
              {
                "uuid": "9db64f30-ab13-46d7-bb5b-abf141a1481b",
                "control-id": "SP_800_171_03.13.08",
                "description": "CUI/PHI is protected cryptographically in transit and in storage. In transit: aws_s3_bucket_policy.uploads denies every s3:* request to the uploads bucket and its objects when aws:SecureTransport is false (GAP-03); the vault, CloudTrail and demo buckets carry the same deny. Clients reach the workload only through the API Gateway HTTP API endpoint, which is HTTPS-only (AWS-managed TLS). The Lambda reaches S3 and DynamoDB over HTTPS (tcp/443) only, through VPC gateway endpoints. In storage: see SP_800_171_03.13.11 (SSE-KMS with the customer CMK). The Rego policy sc_3_13_8_secure_transmission fails the plan when any aws_s3_bucket lacks a bucket policy with a Deny on aws:SecureTransport = false.",
