                    "uuid": "8835eb2f-f3d4-4815-94cf-cdea5a095188",
                    "description": "Every S3 bucket in the system has an explicit aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block with all four flags true. This makes the AWS account default explicit, version-controlled and gate-enforced, so no bucket holding PHI, audit logs or evidence can grant anonymous access. The Rego policy ac_3_1_1_no_public_access fails the plan for any aws_s3_bucket without such a block. Access to the data stores is granted only to the Lambda execution role, and the gateway endpoint policies further limit it to this workload's bucket and table."
